WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.300
Housing financialization.

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.670
When homes became assets.

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:09.409
The median Canadian home price exceeded eight times the median household income.

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:13.500
In Toronto and Vancouver, the ratio exceeds twelve to one.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:17.250
A generation of Canadians has been priced out of homeownership.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.852
This did not happen by accident.

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:27.159
It happened through documented policy choices: CMHC mortgage insurance that backstops five hundred billion in mortgages.

00:00:27.159 --> 00:00:32.488
REIT tax structures that incentivise institutional ownership of residential property.

00:00:32.488 --> 00:00:35.977
Immigration targets that outpace housing construction.

00:00:35.977 --> 00:00:38.772
Zoning restrictions that limit supply.

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:42.238
Foreign buyer programs that were too late and too weak.

00:00:42.238 --> 00:00:45.465
Each mechanism is documented from official data.

00:00:45.465 --> 00:00:53.215
The result: housing as the primary asset class for institutional investors, and shelter as an unaffordable luxury for young Canadians.

00:00:53.215 --> 00:00:56.534
The five mechanisms of housing financialization.

00:00:56.534 --> 00:01:01.306
Each documented from official policy, tax legislation, and market data.

00:01:01.306 --> 00:01:04.715
The institutional architecture of unaffordability.

00:01:04.715 --> 00:01:09.738
Every mechanism that drives housing unaffordability is a government policy decision.

00:01:09.738 --> 00:01:12.659
CMHC insurance: federal.

00:01:12.659 --> 00:01:15.647
REIT tax treatment: federal.

00:01:15.647 --> 00:01:18.136
Immigration targets: federal.

00:01:18.136 --> 00:01:20.806
Capital gains exemption: federal.

00:01:20.806 --> 00:01:25.329
Zoning is municipal but federal funding conditions could incentivise reform.

00:01:25.329 --> 00:01:35.284
The government that created these policies is led by a Prime Minister who came from Brookfield Asset Management — a firm with one of the world's largest infrastructure and real estate portfolios.

00:01:35.284 --> 00:01:44.249
The Crown corporation that insures the mortgages, CMHC, operates with minimal parliamentary oversight as documented in the Crown corporation analysis.

00:01:44.249 --> 00:01:51.397
The regulators that oversee financial institutions are themselves captured as documented in the regulatory capture analysis.

00:01:51.397 --> 00:01:54.340
Every layer of the system is documented.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:59.136
Every policy choice serves institutional investors over Canadian families.
